{
  "$comment": "EXP-1490 (eMCP E1, epic VAPP-175, 2026-10-31): THE VAULT, encryption at rest for every secret column eMCP touches: better-auth `accounts` tokens (`access_token`, `refresh_token`, `id_token`), `mcp_credentials.ciphertext`, the flow verifier and DCR client secret (which today derive their key from BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, lib/mcp-oauth/crypto.ts; E2 moves them here). THE KEY: env `VAULT_KEY` = `<kid>:<standard base64 of 32 random bytes>` (kid matches `kidPattern`); `VAULT_KEYS_RETIRED` = comma-separated keys of the same form, used to OPEN only (`parseKeyring`: null when the current key is missing or malformed, a retired entry is malformed, or a kid repeats; the server refuses to boot the eMCP surfaces without a keyring, `keyringCases`). THE FORMAT (`version` `ev1`): `ev1.<kid>.<iv>.<ciphertext‖tag>`, AES-256-GCM, a fresh random 12-byte iv per seal, the 16-byte tag appended, iv and body base64url without padding. THE AAD binds the value to its row AND the key: `ev1|<kid>|<table>.<column>|<row id>` (UTF-8), so a value copied into another row or column, or relabelled with another kid, does not open (`openCases`). `vaultOpen` → the plaintext or null for anything that does not open (another version, an unknown kid, a wrong slot, a tampered body, a malformed value); null reads as \"not connected\", never as an error. ROTATION: set a new `VAULT_KEY`, move the old one into `VAULT_KEYS_RETIRED`; a daily sweep re-seals every value whose kid is not the current one (`vaultNeedsRotation`), and the retired key can be dropped once the sweep reports none left. `sealVectors` are exact (fixed key and iv): every mirror must produce the same string and open it.",
